    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_062dbe7a4d7b42b5c54254f1f4e318078b8881483d8b1a8bd9c7553c08852d00",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: changing one coordinate c_k updates every affected coefficient a_j in O(n); infeasible states are undone, admissible states are subjected to the annealing rule, and successive inverse-temperature, greedy, and step-shrink phases are diversified across runs. Conceptual interpretation: the coefficient/autocorrelation representation co-designs the constraint test with the search move, gaining cheap incremental state maintenance and allowing every proposal to be screened before scoring, while retaining the limitations of floating-point stochastic optimization. The method assumes the displayed update identities and the coefficient tests correctly represent admissibility; it neither supplies a global-optimum guarantee nor by itself supplies numerical certification, and reproduction still bears the burden of checking the compact indices and arithmetic behavior.",
