    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5618632e4d8bc105b48396800fd8f065b651475b94d670734132570093168aa5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Within the fixed Kadiri calculation, the source attributes most of the realized improvement to the new polynomial together with retained error information, diagnoses the mismatch between the Landau surrogate and R₀, and repairs that mismatch by rescoring and refining candidates under R₀. A separate T₀ sweep with F₁₆ approaches an empirical fitted floor, indicating that certificate and error-bound design offer more leverage here than increasing verified height alone.",
