    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5d711d5e9acd3e4f2ecab4998fc6c1cc5bfd8b86f8e4ec35419d1c2d4acbe524",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The square-modulus representation makes global nonnegativity structural while leaving coefficient constraints explicit; Landau's V objective then supplies a cheap search score, whereas Kadiri's kernel-and-error calculation maps each admissible polynomial to an R₀ bound. Because record-V polynomials do not preserve the R₀ ranking, the source reranks a broad surrogate-selected pool under R₀ and locally refines the target winner.",
